smithy receipt: run a command and record it as evidence for a claim

usage:
  smithy receipt run [--claim "<claim>"] -- <command> [args...]
      runs the command in the repo root, streams its output and records a
      receipt:
      claim, command, exit code, output digest, commit, dirty tree, duration,
      platform.
      Exits with the command's exit code; 127 when the command can't start
      (nothing recorded);
      128+signal when it was killed by a signal, or when smithy itself was
      interrupted (then
      nothing is recorded).
  smithy receipt list [--md] [--all] [--claim <c>]
      receipts for the current commit (--all: every commit); --md prints a table
      for a PR body.
      A receipt taken on another commit is marked stale (unless only task, spec
      or changelog
      files changed since); with uncommitted changes, dirty.
  smithy receipt check-red [--claim repro]
      exit 0 when a receipt with that claim exited non-zero on a commit before
      HEAD (the failing
      reproduction, committed before the fix) and one with that claim passes on
      HEAD; else exit 1
      naming the cause. list also shows such red receipts ("red before fix";
      --claim picks the
      red claim, default repro) and the newest holdout from an earlier commit
      ("holdout commit",
      or "holdout failed").
  smithy receipt clear
Receipts live in <repo>/.smelt/receipts.jsonl; .smelt/ ignores itself (its own
.gitignore).

Examples:
  smithy receipt run -- go test ./...
  smithy receipt run --claim "tests pass" -- npm test
  smithy receipt list --md

See also: smithy help scan, smithy help verify
Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error (3 where a command's help says).
